    "roles": ["band_member", "touring", "session"],
    "summary": "Oasis's drummer from 1995 to 2004, the band's longest-serving: a South Londoner, Steve White's younger brother, taught the Moeller method by Bob Armstrong and raised on soul, sent to Noel Gallagher by Paul Weller. He came in for Morning Glory, and his snare, answering off the beat rather than sitting on 2 and 4, is the rhythm of Wonderwall and Don't Look Back in Anger: 'shuffling away on his snare', said Owen Morris, who thought him a jazz drummer. The rock songs he played straight, as he said they needed. Four albums, most of the B-sides; replaced by Zak Starkey in 2004."
  },
